error[ffi_writable_parameter]: `s1` of `strtok` is declared `cstr`, and the header says `char *` — C does not promise to leave it alone
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-writable-parameter.hero:45:21
     |
  45 |     function strtok(s1: cstr lent, s2: cstr lent) -> cstr  #~ ffi_writable_parameter
     |                     ^^
  note: spec § 13: `s.cstr()` lends a `str` to C, and C writes back through a lend only where the binding is a `@` name. A header's pointer without `const` does not promise that: a C write through it changes the bytes of every value that shares the string, and on a literal's stops the program
  note: declare it `ptr` and give `strtok` a buffer C owns, then read the result back
  fix (guess): declare it `ptr`
